\section{Appendix }

\subsection{Software }

\begin{itemize}




\item \textbf{Microsoft Office:} The raw data regarding the  EBA transparency exercises  was downloaded  from the EBA's official website in .csv or/and .xlsx file formats. Therefore, Microsoft Office products were used.

\item  \textbf{SAS:} SAS software was used to prepare the data sets prior to the empirical analysis, including data collection, cleansing, transformation and storage. SAS is a statistical software suite developed by SAS Institute for data management and advanced analytics. This software is used for some tasks regarding data import, data transformation and relational data in order to set proper data structures.

\item \textbf{Rstudio \& R programming language:} Final data sets are to be provided in .Rdata file format as the proper empirical analysis is performed in R. RStudio is an integrated development environment for R, a programming language for statistical computing and graphics. The generated code in a .rnw file format  will be embedded in a \LaTeX\ document using knitr  (an engine for dynamic report generation with R). R programming language is used in this thesis for graph/chart generation, descriptive statistics and the estimation and inference of parameters in the econometric models.

\item \textbf{TexMaker \& PDF:}
This master's thesis is presented in PDF format. The document was typed in \LaTeX\ (a document preparation system for  high-quality typesetting) and compiled into PDF using PDFLatex. TexMaker is used as \LaTeX\ editor. TexMaker is a free, modern and cross-platform \LaTeX\ editor. This software was used parallel with knitr for the review, enhancement and refinement of \LaTeX\  syntax in the .tex  files generated by knitr.

\end{itemize}

